    "steps": [
      {
        "text": "Pat the fish dry, rub it with the salt and dust it all over with the cornstarch, shaking off the excess.",
        "minutes": null
      },
      {
        "text": "Heat the oil in a wide pan or wok over medium-high heat. Fry the fish until the underside is crisp and golden.",
        "minutes": 7
      },
      {
        "text": "Turn carefully and fry the other side until crisp and the flesh in the scores is opaque. Drain and move to a platter.",
        "minutes": 7
      },
      {
        "text": "In a clean pan, heat the tablespoon of oil over medium heat. Sauté the garlic, ginger and onion until fragrant, then add the bell pepper and carrot and cook for a minute.",
        "minutes": 2
      },
      {
        "text": "Add the vinegar and let it boil without stirring. Then stir in the sugar, ketchup, water and salt and simmer.",
        "minutes": 3
      },
      {
        "text": "Stir the cornstarch mixture, pour it in and stir until the sauce turns glossy and thickens. Taste: it should be equally sweet and sour.",
        "minutes": 1
      },
      {
        "text": "Pour the sauce and vegetables over the fish and serve right away while the skin is still crisp.",
        "minutes": null
      }
    ],
    "tips": "Maya-maya or tilapia work just as well. Make the sauce while the fish fries so both are hot at the same time."
